// @PLN35 golden · P7 (L3.6 iterator input) — GREEN (Phase 7 Path B, step 2a; SCALAR elements).
// Maintained guard: tests/scripts/35p-iterator-match.loft.  A coroutine `iterator<T>` match subject
// is materialised into a buffer `vector<T>` (eager pull — explicit next/exhausted; a `for` over a
// STORED coroutine hangs) and the existing vector-match runs over it, so streaming stays behind the
// Cursor seam (NO OpMatchAnchor/OpMatchRevert needed — the buffer holds all pulled items, so
// backtracking is a free index; the plan's 2 opcodes evaporated).  Text / vector / tuple element
// types ride a different coroutine `next` channel — deferred with a clean diagnostic; a lazy
// per-read pull + max_lookahead is the step-2b refinement.  This golden now RUNS on both backends:

fn count() -> iterator<integer> { yield 1; yield 5; yield 6; }
fn main() {
  r = match count() { [ 1, args:integer* ] => "call/{args.len()}", _ => "?" };
  print("P7 iterator-match: {r}");   // call/2 (both backends)
}
